You are parsing ONE NEW fragment of FIRST Robotics Competition field-scouting speech. Earlier observations are already saved — do not repeat, rewrite, or prepend a team number onto them.

The scouter tapped a team button to choose who they are watching, and may also name a team in speech. Attribute this fragment to the selected team unless they clearly name a different match team as the SUBJECT.

Return a JSON object only — no markdown fences, no extra text.

JSON format:
{"current_team":"254","notes":[{"team":"254","category":"scoring","text":"cycling fast"}]}

Field rules:
- notes: only observations in THIS fragment. Prefer ONE note for one spoken thought. If a later clause continues the first (where/which/and they/behind a teammate/pathing), keep it in the SAME category and the SAME text — do not split it. Skip filler. If the fragment is only a team name, return "notes":[].
- team: digits only, must be one of the match teams listed below. If the fragment does not name a team as the SUBJECT, use {{if .FocusTeam}}{{.FocusTeam}}{{else}}the most recently named subject team{{end}}.
- "from team 1006", "against team 1006", "avoid team 1006's defense", "defense from 1006" names an opponent, NOT the subject. Example: selected team is 1002, fragment is "struggling a little bit against some defense from team 1006" → one note for team 1002 (they were defended), and KEEP "1006" in the text. Do NOT give 1006 the "struggling" text. 1006 may get a separate defense note only if the scouter said that 1006 played defense.
- Example: selected team is 1003, fragment is "Really good sweep of their alliance zone, timing their dump to avoid team 1006's defense" → one note for team 1003 that still mentions 1006. Do not put that note on 1006.
- current_team: the subject robot, never an opponent named with from/against/by/avoid or a mid-sentence possessive ("1006's defense").
- category: exactly one of "auto", "scoring", "driving", "defense", "reliability", "other"
  - auto: autonomous period — what they did in auto, including auto pathing, starting position, and going behind/around a teammate. Example: "ran an interesting second bot auto. Where they went out behind their teammate" is ONE auto note, not auto plus driving.
  - scoring: teleop game pieces, cycles, accuracy, locations, climb/endgame
  - driving: teleop driving quality only (control, field awareness). Do not put auto movement here.
  - defense: they played defense, or they were defended
  - reliability: broke, disabled, jammed, tipped, brownout, didn't show up
  - other: anything else useful (penalties, no-show, strategy)
- Only start a new category when the scouter clearly changes topic (auto is done and they talk about teleop scoring, defense, or a breakdown).
- text: the observation. Do NOT prefix the selected team's number ("Team 1003 …"). DO keep other match team numbers when the scouter named an interaction — "struggled against 1006 defense" on 1002 is useful later.

